      "reason": "A dystopian cyberpunk film whose clandestine psychic experiments and Tetsuo's escalating telekinetic abilities drive an increasingly destructive mystery. The 124-minute film combines sustained violent action, graphic body horror and a grim Neo-Tokyo setting with exceptionally distinctive hand-drawn animation. The investigation and revelation of Akira's nature are meaningful, but psychological out-thinking and a formal trainable power system are weaker than its spectacle; a substantial military presence and retro visual language are also relevant limitations. The feature's overall action intensity and graphic violence are supported by whole-film reviews rather than trailer footage.",
